{"name":"Cortex","hex":"#a99592","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cortex","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The outer layer of an internal organ or body structure, such as the kidney or the brain.","The tissue of a stem or root that lies inward from the epidermis, but exterior to the vascular tissue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cortex"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cortex (anatomy)","blocks":[{"text":"In anatomy and zoology, the cortex is the outermost, otherwise known as superficial, layer of an organ. Organs with well-defined cortical layers include kidneys, adrenal glands, ovaries, the thymus, and the brain, including the cerebellar cortex and the cerebral cortex the best-known of all cortices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Brainmaps-macaque-hippocampus.jpg/330px-Brainmaps-macaque-hippocampus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cortex_(anatomy)","wikidata":"Q2346577"},{"title":"Cerebral cortex","blocks":[{"text":"The cerebral cortex, also known as the cerebral mantle, is the outer layer of neural tissue of the cerebrum of the brain in humans and other mammals. It is the largest site of neural integration in the central nervous system, and plays a key role in attention, perception, awareness, thought, memory, language, and consciousness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Cerebral_cortex%2C_side_view.svg/330px-Cerebral_cortex%2C_side_view.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerebral_cortex","wikidata":"Q75839"},{"title":"Cortex (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Cortex is a French jazz funk band formed by band leader Alain Mion in 1974. Cortex is known for polyrhythmic instrumentals and funk, bossa nova, samba-jazz, and psychedelic rock grooves, mixed with atmospheric vocals, inspired by 1970s American funk and jazz. Cortex broke up in 1981, but reformed in 2009 with a rotating group of members. Hip hop samples of Cortex songs in tracks from artists including MF Doom, Madlib, Tyler, the Creator, Kanye West, Flying Lotus, Lupe Fiasco, and Suicideboys have brought newfound interest to the band starting in the early 2000s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Cortex_band_members_June_2024.jpg/330px-Cortex_band_members_June_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cortex_(band)","wikidata":"Q121461533"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Illu_kidney.jpg/250px-Illu_kidney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/Illu_kidney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Illu_kidney.jpg/250px-Illu_kidney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The renal cortex, here denoted by the number 2.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllu_kidney.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Blausen_0103_Brain_Sensory%26Motor.png/500px-Blausen_0103_Brain_Sensory%26Motor.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Blausen_0103_Brain_Sensory%26Motor.png/1280px-Blausen_0103_Brain_Sensory%26Motor.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Blausen_0103_Brain_Sensory%26Motor.png/500px-Blausen_0103_Brain_Sensory%26Motor.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlausen_0103_Brain_Sensory%26Motor.p